= Distribution shift — Simple =

'''Distribution shift''' happens when the data a model sees later are different from the data it learned from.

For example, a spam filter trained on old messages may face new styles of spam.

A medical model trained at one hospital may see different equipment or patient populations elsewhere.

This is different from ordinary overfitting.

A model can perform well on fresh data from the old distribution and still fail when the environment changes.

